The five draft layers have indices zero through four. The hidden size is 5120 and the vocabulary size is 248320.
The baseline uses selector_rank=256, two convolution taps [0,1], group_size=16, and no correctors.
The architecture object contains exactly convolutions and correctors lists.
A convolution record selects one layer and either the attention or mlp sublayer.
Its taps are sorted unique positions from zero through seven and include zero and one.
Its group_size is eight or sixteen. The physical tap allocation is max(taps)+1, including excluded zero slots.
The new tap coefficients start at zero. Finer groups retain the learned coarse coefficients.
Excluded taps remain zero during training and serving. Do not count excluded slots as free parameters.
A corrector record selects one layer, a rank from 32/64/128/256, and a Boolean gated value.
It adds up(SiLU(down(h))*sigmoid(gate(h))) when gated, or up(SiLU(down(h))) otherwise.
The down and up projections have no bias. The optional gate projects the complete hidden state to one scalar.
The up projection and optional gate weights start at zero. The initial sigmoid is 0.5, not a saturated random gate.
Native gradient and strict checkpoint gates must pass.
Use at most one convolution per layer/sublayer and one corrector per layer. Do not declare unchanged convolutions.

Choose selector_rank=256 or 384. Rank expansion is optional, not the sole architecture change.
Require at least one convolution or corrector. Do not repeat the completed rank-only screen.
Keep learning_rate=0.00003, selector_loss_weight=0.1, and seed=42.
The released draft has 1,924,404,480 actual parameters. Total growth cannot exceed five percent of that count.
Rank 384 adds 64,225,280 parameters. Count this growth together with every other component.
A corrector adds 2*5120*rank parameters, plus 5120 for a gate.
A convolution with K physical taps and G=5120/group_size has 2*K*5120 + 2*K*G*5120 parameters.
Subtract the replaced two-tap, group-16 convolution count. The CPU estimate must match the native physical count.
Inherited coefficients use the original 1280-row GEMM shape. Extra taps use a separate projection.
Finer groups use independent inherited projections, then interleave the coefficients. Account for these extra GEMM launches in your compute tradeoff.
